    "title": "AI Could Make Small Trade Loans Pay Off Again",
    "summary": "When a company sells goods to a buyer overseas, it often has to wait 30, 60 or 90 days to get paid. In the meantime, it needs cash to keep running. Banks have historically been reluctant to lend against that wait, especially for smaller companies, because the cost of checking a borrower’s paperwork and creditworthiness […]\nThe post AI Could Make Small Trade Loans Pay Off Again appeared first on PYMNTS.com.",
    "hasSummary": true,
    "link": "https://www.pymnts.com/loans/working-capital/2026/ai-could-make-small-trade-loans-pay-off-again/",
    "source": "PYMNTS",
    "tags": [
      "PYMNTS.com"
    ],
    "origin": "rss",
    "pubDate": "2026-09-02T21:22:23.000Z",
    "fetchedAt": "2026-09-02T22:39:40.374Z",
    "isDuplicateOf": null,
    "content": "Companies selling goods overseas often wait up to 90 days to receive payment, creating cash flow challenges. Historically, banks have been reluctant to provide small trade loans to smaller companies because the manual cost of verifying paperwork and creditworthiness is too high. Artificial intelligence may now help reduce these administrative costs, potentially making small trade loans profitable and accessible again.",
